    "type": "function",
    "function": {
      "name": "task",
      "description": "Custom agent: Launch specialized agents in separate context windows for specific tasks.\n\nThe Task tool launches specialized agents that autonomously handle complex tasks. Each agent type has specific capabilities and tools available to it.\n\nAvailable agent types:\n- **explore**: Fast agent specialized for exploring codebases and answering questions about code. Use this when you need to quickly find files by patterns (eg. \"src/components/**/*.tsx\"), search code for keywords (eg. \"API endpoints\"), or answer questions about the codebase (eg. \"how do API endpoints work?\", \"what does this codebase do?\", \"where is authentication logic?\"). Answers multi-part questions thoroughly. Safe to call in parallel — batch related questions into one call or launch multiple in parallel. (Tools: grep/glob/view/bash/powershell, Haiku model)\n\n- **task**: Agent for executing commands with verbose output (tests, builds, lints, dependency installs). Returns brief summary on success (\"All 247 tests passed\", \"Build succeeded\"), full output on failure (stack traces, compiler errors). Keeps main context clean by minimizing successful output. Use for tasks where you only need to know success/failure status. (Tools: All CLI tools, Haiku model)\n\n- **general-purpose**: Full-capability agent running in a subprocess. Use for complex multi-step tasks requiring the complete toolset and high-quality reasoning. Runs in a separate context window to keep your main conversation clean. (Tools: All CLI tools, Sonnet model)\n\n- **code-review**: Agent for reviewing code changes with extremely high signal-to-noise ratio. Analyzes staged/unstaged changes and branch diffs. Only surfaces issues that genuinely matter - bugs, security vulnerabilities, logic errors. Never comments on style, formatting, or trivial matters. Will NOT modify code. (Tools: All CLI tools for investigation)\n\n- **configure-copilot**: Agent for managing Copilot CLI MCP server configuration. Use when the user wants to add, remove, or modify MCP servers. Edits config files and reloads servers automatically.\n\nUser-provided custom agents:\n\nThese are custom agents configured specifically for your environment. They may have specialized knowledge, tools, or workflows tailored to your project needs.\n\n- **agent-factory-explorer**: Explores the workspace to discover existing agents, skills, MCP servers, conventions, and infrastructure patterns relevant to building a new agent family.\n\n- **agent-factory-family-auditor**: Audits the full family and produces a local repair plan when the family still needs refinement.\n\n- **agent-factory-family-integrator**: Verifies whole-family completeness and assembles the pass-level family summary before the final family audit.\n\n- **agent-factory-orchestrator-auditor**: Audits the built orchestrator for purity, routing completeness, and correct control-file usage.\n\n- **agent-factory-orchestrator-builder**: Builds the top-level orchestrator once all component prompts and skills are ready.\n\n- **agent-factory-roster-architect**: Designs the family roster, workflow shape, skill inventory, and control-file queues before any implementation starts.\n\n- **agent-factory-roster-auditor**: Audits the family roster before any implementation begins.\n\n- **agent-factory-skill-architect**: Designs one required new skill at a time from the approved roster.\n\n- **agent-factory-skill-auditor**: Audits one skill at a time against its approved skill spec.\n\n- **agent-factory-skill-builder**: Builds one skill at a time from an approved skill spec.\n\n- **agent-factory-subagent-architect**: Designs one subagent spec at a time from the approved roster.\n\n- **agent-factory-subagent-auditor**: Audits one subagent specification at a time before it is built.\n\n- **agent-factory-subagent-build-auditor**: Audits one built subagent file at a time against its approved spec.\n\n- **agent-factory-subagent-builder**: Builds one subagent prompt file at a time from an approved spec.\n\n- **agent-factory**: Autonomous agent that creates complete agent-as-function families. Takes a description of what the agent should do and produces orchestrator, subagents, skills, and routing infrastructure.\n\n- **builder-implementer**: Implements one phase of an implementation plan — creates and modifies files as specified.\n\n- **builder-planner**: Parses phased implementation plans into a structured execution plan for the builder orchestrator.\n\n- **builder-reviewer**: Reviews implementer changes against the plan phase to verify correctness and compliance.\n\n- **builder-scribe**: Writes completion report summarizing plan execution results across all phases.\n\n- **builder-verifier**: Runs the plan verification checklist after all phases complete to validate end-to-end correctness.\n\n- **builder**: Autonomous orchestrator that executes phased implementation plans by dispatching subagents.\n\n- **docwriter-accuracy-reviewer**: Verifies every technical claim in written content against actual source code.\n\n- **docwriter-analysis-coordinator**: Analysis-planning coordinator — dispatches code analysis, invariant scanning, impact mapping, task planning, and risk analysis.\n\n- **docwriter-architecture**: Deep-dive architecture reference for the docwriter fractal pipeline — artifact flow, design decisions, agent interactions.\n\n- **docwriter-changelog-writer**: Writes a release notes / changelog entry summarizing all documentation changes from the pipeline run.\n\n- **docwriter-code-analyzer**: Deep code comprehension — traces call chains and extracts behavioral impact for every changed file.\n\n- **docwriter-content-writer**: Writes or updates a single documentation page per invocation, following inlined invariants and docFacts.\n\n- **docwriter-corpus-scanner**: Scans entire doc workspace, indexes every page with front matter, headings, cross-references, and topic clusters.\n\n- **docwriter-cross-ref-updater**: Finds and updates cross-references in pages linking to/from modified documentation pages.\n\n- **docwriter-delivery-coordinator**: Delivery coordinator — dispatches front matter validation, changelog writing, and PR preparation.\n\n- **docwriter-diff-analyzer**: Parses Git diff, categorizes changes by product area, emits structured change inventory.\n\n- **docwriter-discovery-coordinator**: Discovery coordinator — dispatches diff-analyzer and corpus-scanner, validates outputs.\n\n- **docwriter-execution-coordinator**: Execution coordinator — orchestrates the content-writer → triple-reviewer loop for each documentation task.\n\n- **docwriter-frontmatter-validator**: Validates Jekyll front matter, Liquid syntax, and build readiness for all created/modified doc files.\n\n- **docwriter-gap-hunter**: Adversarial completeness audit — finds undocumented changes, stale content, and invariant enforcement gaps.\n\n- **docwriter-guide**: User guide for the docwriter agent family — prints documentation and answers questions about the pipeline.\n\n- **docwriter-impact-mapper**: Cross-references code changes with doc corpus to determine which pages need updates, new pages, or stale-content fixes.\n\n- **docwriter-invariant-scanner**: Reads all guidelines files, extracts enforceable rules with unique IDs into a structured invariant inventory.\n\n- **docwriter-persona-reviewer**: Reviews documentation for correct persona targeting, audience-appropriate tone/depth, and taxonomy compliance.\n\n- **docwriter-pr-preparer**: Stages all doc changes on a git branch, writes PR description, creates commit.\n\n- **docwriter-risk-analyzer**: Assesses risk across 5 dimensions for each planned documentation task.\n\n- **docwriter-style-reviewer**: Reviews documentation for style guide compliance, structural conventions, Jekyll formatting, and cross-ref syntax.\n\n- **docwriter-task-planner**: Converts impact matrix into dependency-ordered task graph with inlined invariants per task.\n\n- **docwriter-verification-coordinator**: Verification coordinator — dispatches cross-ref updater and gap hunter, manages convergence loop.\n\n- **docwriter**: Fractal documentation orchestrator — routes a 7-pass doc pipeline via coordinator status.json files.\n\n- **migration-api-mapper**: Maps API endpoints, controllers, and contracts into the feature inventory.\n\n- **migration-coder**: Implements one migration slice at a time — reads slice spec, writes migrated code.\n\n- **migration-config-mapper**: Maps configuration files, environment variables, and feature flags into the feature inventory.\n\n- **migration-contract-validator**: Diffs API contracts between old and new systems — URL patterns, payloads, status codes, error shapes.\n\n- **migration-data-mapper**: Maps data models, schemas, and database migrations into the feature inventory.\n\n- **migration-delivery-coordinator**: Delivery coordinator — dispatches hardening, documentation, and handoff agents sequentially.\n\n- **migration-dependency-analyzer**: Builds directed dependency graph between features and identifies migration clusters.\n\n- **migration-discovery-coordinator**: Discovery coordinator — dispatches 6 domain mappers and validates feature-inventory completeness.\n\n- **migration-documentation-writer**: Documentation writer — produces decision log, changelog, and migration notes from artifacts.\n\n- **migration-execution-coordinator**: Execution coordinator — routes coder→reviewer→test-writer loop per migration slice.\n\n- **migration-feature-mapper**: Maps UI components, pages, views, and layouts into the feature inventory.\n\n- **migration-gap-hunter**: Adversarial gap-hunter — searches the full codebase for missed features, hidden behaviors, and incomplete invariant coverage.\n\n- **migration-handoff-writer**: Handoff writer — produces the final delivery summary with coverage, outstanding items, and recommendations.\n\n- **migration-hardening-checker**: Hardening checker — verifies production readiness: performance, resilience, accessibility, observability, rollback.\n\n- **migration-job-mapper**: Maps background jobs, cron tasks, and worker processes into the feature inventory.\n\n- **migration-journey-validator**: Runs Playwright user journey comparisons between old and new systems per slice.\n\n- **migration-parity-checker**: Aggregates oracle results per slice and determines verified/failed-parity status.\n\n- **migration-planning-coordinator**: Planning coordinator — routes semantics analysis (Pass 2) and planning (Pass 3) phases.\n\n- **migration-reviewer**: Reviews coder output against invariants, acceptance criteria, and error paths. Approves or rejects.\n\n- **migration-risk-analyzer**: Assesses migration risk per slice across 6 categories and writes mitigation plans.\n\n- **migration-route-mapper**: Maps routes, navigation flows, and URL patterns into the feature inventory.\n\n- **migration-semantics-analyzer**: Extracts behavioral semantics — state transitions, validation rules, auth rules, error paths, invariants — per feature.\n\n- **migration-slice-planner**: Decomposes analyzed features into dependency-ordered migration slices with inline invariants.\n\n- **migration-test-writer**: Writes runnable tests for each migrated slice — invariants, error paths, and happy paths.\n\n- **migration-verification-coordinator**: Verification coordinator — inline per-slice oracle dispatch and gap-hunting batch mode.\n\n- **migration**: Fractal migration orchestrator — routes a 7-pass migration pipeline via coordinator status.json files.\n\n- **planner**: Researches change requests, asks clarifying questions, and produces specification, plan, and task breakdown files\n\n- **ralph.malph-reviewer-gemini**: Independent PR reviewer (Gemini model) — runs the full review checklist and posts findings to ADO PR\n\n- **ralph.malph-reviewer-gpt**: Independent PR reviewer (GPT model) — runs the full review checklist and posts findings to ADO PR\n\n- **ralph.malph-reviewer-opus**: Independent PR reviewer (Opus model) — runs the full review checklist and posts findings to ADO PR\n\n- **ralph.malph-scout**: Review scout sub-agent — pre-reads the PR diff, maps changes to codebase patterns, and runs build validation\n\n- **ralph.malph**: Multi-model review orchestrator — dispatches scout + 3 independent reviewers + scribe\n\n- **ralph.ralph-analyst**: Analyzes JIRA issues and suggests implementation paths for the Kentico Docs VS Code extension.\n\n- **ralph.ralph-coder**: Implements code changes for the Kentico Docs VS Code extension based on an analyst implementation plan.\n\n- **ralph.ralph-planner**: Planning sub-agent — breaks analyst implementation plans into ordered task files for per-task coder→reviewer execution\n\n- **ralph.ralph-reviewer**: Reviews code changes made by the coder agent for the Kentico Docs VS Code extension.\n\n- **ralph.ralph-scribe**: Reads all subagent artifacts and posts a synthesis to the Ralphchives knowledge base.\n\n- **ralph.ralph**: Autonomous orchestrator that routes subagents to develop vscode extensions.\n\n- **ralph.robinson-explorer**: Architecture explorer helper — maps feature ownership, execution flow, and integration points for VS Code extension tasks.\n\n- **ralph.scientist-agent-improver**: Post-task hook — proposes agent infrastructure improvements based on analysis\n\n- **ralph.scientist-run-analyzer**: Post-task hook — analyzes completed agent execution logs\n\n- **ralph.scientist**: Post-task orchestrator — dispatches run-analyzer then agent-improver to produce execution analysis and improvements\n\n- **ralph.vasco-explorer**: Pattern explorer helper — finds analogous implementations, tests, grammar touchpoints, and edge cases for VS Code extension tasks.\n\nWhen NOT to use Task tool:\n- Reading specific file paths you already know - use view tool instead\n- Simple single grep/glob search - use grep/glob tools directly\n- Commands where you need immediate full output in your context - use bash directly\n- File operations on known files - use edit/create tools directly\n\nUsage notes:\n- Can launch multiple explore/code-review agents in parallel (task, general-purpose, configure-copilot have side effects)\n- Each agent is stateless - provide complete context in your prompt\n- Agent results are returned in a single message\n- Use explore proactively for codebase questions before making changes\n- Use 'model' parameter to override the default model (18 models available)",
